# Git for Windows checks out with CRLF by default, which breaks the container
# setup in a way that gives no useful error.
#
# `docker/restore-dump.sh` is bind-mounted into the Postgres container and run
# there by bash. With a CR at the end of every line, `set -euo pipefail` fails
# as `pipefail\r: invalid option name`; the init script aborts under `set -e`;
# the TCP healthcheck never goes green; and `app`, which waits on
# `service_healthy`, hangs forever with the cause buried in the db logs.
#
# So: LF on every platform, whatever the local `core.autocrlf` says.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reason, one step removed. The Dockerfile parser tolerates CRLF today,
# but a `RUN` carrying a heredoc would hand those CRs straight to a shell.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
